Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Use typed float Skia working buffers without changing
 Canvas formats

Allocate non-Canvas Skia working surfaces in extended nonlinear-sRGB-capable F16 storage with actual stride and memory accounting. Keep logical pixel-buffer APIs at their existing formats and convert through Skia instead of copying raw float bytes. Preserve float pattern and luminance-mask intermediates while retaining normal unsupported-renderer fallback.

Source implementation only; native compile, vtable/link and behavioral checks remain pending coordinator admission.
